# Gargantuan Leech ({7}{B}, 5/5 lifelink): "This spell costs {1} less to cast for each Cave you control and each Cave card in your graveyard." Bot1 sacrifices its Promising Vein on turn 3 (one Cave card
# in the graveyard) and has played the Veins on turns 3 and 5 (two Caves on the battlefield): three in all, so the Leech costs {4}{B}, five mana. Four sources are not enough (the refusal; nothing else is
# offerable then) and the fifth, a Mox Ruby, pays exactly: the pool is empty right after the cast (CR 601.2f, 118.7a). Two counted for the battlefield alone, or one for the graveyard alone, would leave mana over.
